  "configuration_id": "config_043",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA is the dominant modality (0.591 RNA-only vs 0.208 image-only), and our best config (config_019, acc=0.639) uses pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder. However, we have zero evidence on whether a learned/non-linear RNA encoder (scgpt or scvi_n200) could improve over linear PCA. This is the highest-leverage untested design axis since RNA drives most of the signal. Question: Does replacing PCA with the pre-trained generative scgpt encoder improve multimodal performance, holding all other settings at their known-best values (multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, weighted fusion)? Why this is the best next experiment: config_043 is a clean single-variable swap from config_019, so any performance delta is attributable to the RNA encoder. A positive result would justify further exploration of learned encoders across all multimodal configs; a null or negative result would confirm PCA sufficiency and redirect budget toward other axes (e.g., transformer aggregation in multimodal, or singleprofile multimodal). This maximizes information gain per experiment under the limited budget."
}

